{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdJvpnGHZNeHM78F2oYuV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-273 is complete and committed. Summary:\n\n## WI-273 — Dashboard semantic tabs (ARIA tabs pattern) — DONE\n\n**Committed:** `912356b` on `llm/train/3-g3-WI-273-b45e`, trailers `WI: WI-273 / Train: 3-g3-WI-273-b45e / Base: 747f1529…`\n\n**What shipped** (closing repo-review M-3 / SR-052): the `PROJECT_STATE.html` view switcher went from visual-only `.active` buttons to a real WAI-ARIA tablist:\n- `role=\"tablist\"`/`role=\"tab\"`/`role=\"tabpanel\"` with `aria-selected`, `aria-controls`, `aria-labelledby`, a roving `tabindex`, and the initial (arch) tab as the sole tab stop.\n- Two emit helpers (`tab_button`/`tab_panel_open`) give the four dynamic tabs the identical wiring, replacing ad-hoc string literals so a future tab can't skip the pattern.\n- A `selectTab` controller keeps `aria-selected` + panel visibility (`.active` **and** `hidden`, toggled oppositely) + roving tabindex in sync, with Left/Right/Up/Down (wrap), Home/End, and Enter/Space keyboard support.\n\n**Verification:** 5 new tests + helper coverage (tablist markup, extra-tab semantics, tab↔panel bijection, keyboard controller, helpers). Ruff clean; `check_docs --stale` exit 0; pre-commit floor all PASS; **full suite 1343 passed, 39 skipped**. I also regenerated the dashboard from live data and confirmed 5 tabs ↔ 5 panels, one selected, bijection holds.\n\n**Handled along the way:**\n- **Module-size ratchet** (`gen_trajectory.py` 4511→4573): a reviewed UPWARD baseline re-stamp per the ratchet's own escape hatch, reason named inline + in the commit (WI-280 decomposition is deferred).\n- **Generated artifacts** (`docs/architecture.md` map + `PROJECT_STATE.html`) were regenerated via the canonical tools to pass the universal pre-commit floor — the integrator re-regenerates them on the composed tree (matching the WI-219 dashboard worker precedent).\n\n**Two things for the integrator/reviewer (flagged in the commit, not buried):**\n1. **Independent critique required.** SR-052 is `Verification=Critique`. This render change re-fires the WI-243 perceptual gate (WARN at commit bar, **ERROR at G3**). It needs a fresh, **independent, family-heterogeneous** dashboard-accessibility critique to clear — which I (the Claude builder) structurally cannot self-certify.\n2. **One pre-existing red, not mine:** `test_forward_only_unit_over_the_real_meta_repo` fires because `docs/status.md` still names the just-integrated `done` WI-275. It reads only coordination-truth files this WI never touched; it's the integrator's `status.md` regen to reconcile.\n\nThe untracked `docs/iteration/*.log` is session-001 harness telemetry — left for the harness, not part of the deliverable."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":416,"cache_read_input_tokens":177817,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":416},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c33a8229-9173-4168-8d0e-2fadb9f09bc3","uuid":"420b3a28-9f2e-4b8b-87e4-a1419c0dd2b7","request_id":"req_011CdJvpjzN7K4oR9xmxWLTe"}
